    description: "Since format arail-roles/3 every role has its party (the organisation or group it belongs to), its scale and horizon (the rhythm of its routine decisions and how far they reach) and its gives: the flows (flows.js) it hands to other roles, each with what exactly is handed over and the roles it goes to. What a role takes is what the others give it. Every pair of roles that work with each other exchanges at least one flow. These flows are the wiring of the big game: a game's ports are a part of its role's flows. The data is web/game/roles/roles.json (format arail-roles/3), loaded where it is needed: the roles page, the career planner, the guide docs/roles.md written by tools/roles-md.mjs, the tests. Each role's access says whether it is a job, how it is filled, a minimum age, the fitness, its ways in (alternatives of qualifications and years in other roles) and what is gained in it; the catalogue's qualifications (school certificates, apprenticeships, degrees, trainings, licences, certificates, exams) say what each needs first. A role's typical moves (career from and to) are hints, drawn as a graph.",
