    summary: "Malus Month (Pönale): the transport authority's contract manager, one round an accounting period of a transport contract. The operator's incident list by classes; for each, what is paid and what a penalty applies to; the operator's objections; an operator that must neither be bled nor spoiled.",
    description: "The rule to learn: train-km not run are not paid, whatever the cause; a penalty on top applies only to causes in the operator's sphere. In the review each class of the period's list is decided (not paid and a penalty, not paid, paid in full; or a penalty or none), and now and then an objection of the operator: justified when its evidence shows a cause outside its sphere. The game computes the account by the rule and compares the player's with it. A penalty waived without a reason, or km not run paid, is found by the auditor; a penalty outside the operator's sphere is lost in the dispute. The operator's finances fall with the penalties and faster with deductions beyond the contract: below a threshold it cuts its own reserves (more failures), at zero it is insolvent and an emergency award follows. Leniency lets its failures grow. In the plan phase the penalty catalogue goes out as the transport contract, and one question is decided: quality checks, or a reduced emergency timetable in a staff shortage. In a session the list's rates follow the reports of the sampled shift (the undertaking's and the signaller's), counted a quarter against the usual ones.",
